# Firewall-Mon deployment overrides. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust.
# docker-compose auto-loads `.env` from the same directory; values referenced
# as ${VAR:-default} in docker-compose.yml pick up these settings.

# ---------- Data volume ----------
# Host path bind-mounted into the container at /data. This holds SQLite (dev)
# or the Postgres PGDATA (prod), plus the config-backup archive. Default in
# the compose file is a project-local ./data dir. Production should point
# this at a dedicated partition with adequate free space — the rust-01
# deployment outgrew the root volume in 2026-05 and was relocated to
# /mnt/STORAGE (see CHANGELOG v0.10.199).
#
# DATA_DIR=/mnt/STORAGE/firewall-mon-data

# ---------- Config volume (ENCRYPTION-KEY CONTINUITY) ----------
# Host path bind-mounted at /config, holding config.env. On first run
# entrypoint.sh writes a RANDOM JWT_SECRET_KEY here if you didn't supply one,
# and the AES-256 key that encrypts every {enc} secret (SNMP/IRC/SMTP creds) is
# derived from it. THIS DIRECTORY MUST PERSIST AND MUST MOVE TOGETHER WITH
# DATA_DIR. If you relocate DATA_DIR to a new path but leave CONFIG_DIR pointing
# at a fresh (empty) dir, a new key is generated and every stored credential in
# the relocated database becomes permanently undecryptable (polling silently
# breaks). Safest of all: set JWT_SECRET_KEY (or ENCRYPTION_KEY) explicitly below
# so key continuity never depends on a bind-mount surviving.
#
# CONFIG_DIR=/mnt/STORAGE/firewall-mon-config

# ---------- Encryption key (recommended explicit pin) ----------
# Pin the key derivation so {enc} secrets survive ANY relocation/redeploy.
# Generate once: `openssl rand -base64 32`. Keep it secret and stable.
#
# Leaving these unset is safe and is the default: the container then derives the
# key from /config/config.env exactly as before. Setting them here takes
# precedence over that file. Before v0.11.180 the compose file did not pass
# these through at all, so setting them here had no effect.
#
# JWT_SECRET_KEY=
# ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------- Image name ----------
# Which image the compose file runs. Default is the Docker Hub tag published by
# CI. A from-source deployment that builds locally under a different tag can
# point at it here instead of editing docker-compose.yml — an edited compose
# file is untracked working-tree drift that makes `git pull` refuse to update
# the deployment checkout.
#
# FIREWALL_MON_IMAGE=firewall-mon:latest
